From forkd_dump Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Mon, 11 May 2026 17:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/a2xx: diagnostic VSC pipe BO dump (FD2_VSC_DUMP env)

Per-hash kernel debugfs (vgt + sq) captured 2026-05-11 confirmed all 8
period-cycle hashes produce BYTE-IDENTICAL register state. The cycle
source is therefore NOT in any MMIO register — must be in either:
  - The actual VSC pipe BO byte contents (binner wrote different
    visibility streams per cycle phase, even with constant DATA_LENGTH)
  - Internal hardware state machines hidden from the register interface

This patch adds CPU-side dumping of the first 4KB of each VSC pipe BO
at the START of fd2_emit_tile_init (before BOs are re-used). Enabled
via env var FD2_VSC_DUMP. Output: /tmp/vsc_pipe<P>_batch<N>.dump.

First batch in a process dumps zeros (BOs newly allocated). Second and
subsequent batches dump the previous batch's binner output. The
companion gl-cap-and-regdump-mainline.c change renders the test
triangle twice per invocation when FD2_VSC_DUMP is set, so each
invocation produces a batch-0 (empty) + batch-1 (real binner output)
dump pair.

If batch-1 bytes vary across the 8 cycle hashes, the binner IS cycling
internally. If batch-1 bytes are byte-identical across hashes, the
cycle is downstream of the binner (rasterizer/RB latched state).

NO functional change to rendering when env var unset.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [diagnostic only]
---
 src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_gmem.c | 37 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 37 insertions(+)

--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_gmem.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_gmem.c
@@ -703,6 +703,43 @@
    if (is_a22x(ctx->screen)) {
       const unsigned num_pipes = 8;
 
+      /* DIAGNOSTIC: dump VSC pipe BO contents from the PREVIOUS batch
+       * (which contains the binner's visibility stream output for that
+       * batch's tile geometry) before we re-use the BOs for this batch.
+       *
+       * Enabled when env var FD2_VSC_DUMP is set. First batch in a
+       * process will dump zeros (BOs freshly allocated below); the
+       * second and subsequent batches will see the prior binner output.
+       *
+       * Output: /tmp/vsc_pipe<P>_batch<N>.dump (first 4KB per pipe).
+       *
+       * Used to determine whether the period-8 render cycle has its
+       * source in the binner (different VSC byte content per phase)
+       * or downstream (rasterizer/RB processing same binner data
+       * differently each cycle).
+       */
+      static int dump_batch_counter = 0;
+      if (getenv("FD2_VSC_DUMP")) {
+         for (int i = 0; i < num_pipes; i++) {
+            if (!ctx->vsc_pipe_bo[i])
+               continue;
+            /* Wait for GPU to finish any pending writes to this BO. */
+            fd_bo_cpu_prep(ctx->vsc_pipe_bo[i], ctx->pipe, FD_BO_PREP_READ);
+            void *map = fd_bo_map(ctx->vsc_pipe_bo[i]);
+            if (!map)
+               continue;
+            char path[64];
+            snprintf(path, sizeof(path), "/tmp/vsc_pipe%d_batch%d.dump",
+                     i, dump_batch_counter);
+            FILE *f = fopen(path, "wb");
+            if (f) {
+               fwrite(map, 4096, 1, f);
+               fclose(f);
+            }
+         }
+         dump_batch_counter++;
+      }
+
       /* Allocate one 256KB VSC pipe BO per pipe (matches webOS initial
        * allocation in leia_binning_grow_vis_stream_buffer). Buffers are
        * reused across batches; grown lazily if a future patch tracks
